<!-- ============================================================
     SAP Commerce Cloud CVE-2026-44761 Detection Rules
     MITRE ATT&amp;CK Techniques:
       T1190  - Exploit Public-Facing Application (TA0001 Initial Access)
       T1078  - Valid Accounts: use of hardcoded sample OAuth2 credentials (TA0001)
       T1530  - Data from Cloud Storage: OCC API data exfiltration (TA0009)
     Rule IDs: 104175-104183
     Author: SecOps Engineer (Purple Team, ESKA-1075)
     Date: 2026-11-02
     CVE: CVE-2026-44761

     Vulnerability Summary:

     CVE-2026-44761 is a Use of Hard-coded Credentials (CWE-798) vulnerability
     in SAP Commerce Cloud (formerly SAP Hybris). SAP ships sample OAuth2
     client credentials (used in development scripts on the SAP Help Portal)
     that remain enabled in production deployments unless explicitly removed.
     CVSS 9.1 (Critical). Affected products: HY_COM 2205, COM_CLOUD 2211,
     COM_CLOUD 2211-JDK21.

     An unauthenticated attacker with network access to the SAP Commerce
     authorization server can:
       1. POST to /authorizationserver/oauth/token with a known sample
          client ID and client secret (no prior knowledge of environment
          required - credentials are publicly documented).
       2. Receive a valid OAuth2 access token granting API access.
       3. Use the token to call SAP Commerce OCC (Omni Commerce Connect)
          REST APIs with high confidentiality and integrity impact:
          read customer order data, product catalog, pricing; modify
          orders, cart contents, or product listings.

     Known hardcoded sample client IDs (publicly documented in SAP Help Portal):
       - mobile_android   (client_credentials and password grant types)
       - trusted_client   (client_credentials grant type)
       - client-side      (implicit and password grant types)

     Attack Flow:
       1. Attacker probes /authorizationserver/oauth/token endpoint.
       2. POST with grant_type=client_credentials, client_id=mobile_android
          (or trusted_client), client_secret=[known sample secret].
       3. Commerce Cloud returns HTTP 200 with access_token JSON payload.
       4. Attacker includes token in Authorization: Bearer [token] header
          on subsequent calls to /occ/v2/ REST API endpoints.
       5. Data exfiltration or catalog manipulation via OCC API.

     Detection Approach:

       104175 (Level 5)  - Base anchor: any POST to the SAP Commerce OAuth2
                           token endpoint. Used for correlation only.
       104176 (Level 14) - Known sample client ID in OAuth2 request URL
                           query parameters (core CVE-2026-44761 signal).
       104177 (Level 12) - OAuth2 token endpoint returns HTTP 200 (successful
                           token issuance - possible exploitation).
       104178 (Level 15) - OAuth2 token successfully granted to known sample
                           client ID (200 response on 104176 match).
       104179 (Level 12) - Burst of OAuth2 token requests from same source
                           (automated exploit tool or scanner).
       104180 (Level 10) - SAP Commerce OCC API path accessed (post-exploit
                           data access indicator).
       104181 (Level 13) - Bulk OCC API enumeration from same source
                           (data exfiltration pattern).
       104182 (Level 9)  - Off-hours OAuth2 request to SAP Commerce
                           (behavioral anomaly, correlate with other signals).
       104183 (Level 13) - SAP Commerce application log OAuth2 token issued
                           to known sample client ID (hybris/Tomcat log source).

     Log Source Prerequisites:

     Rules 104175-104182 target Traefik JSON access logs forwarded to Wazuh
     (decoded_as=json). Required Traefik JSON fields:
       RequestMethod, RequestPath, ClientHost, DownstreamStatus
     If SAP Commerce Cloud is behind Traefik with JSON access logging enabled,
     these rules will fire on matching requests.

     Rule 104183 targets SAP Commerce hybris application logs (Java process
     log, typically from hybris server or Tomcat) forwarded via Wazuh
     localfile monitoring. SAP Commerce logs OAuth2 token grants with the
     client_id in the application log.

     If SAP Commerce Cloud is not deployed in the environment, these rules
     are precautionary and will not produce alerts. Deploy now so coverage
     is in place if an SAP Commerce instance is onboarded or discovered.

     References:
       - CVE-2026-44761: CWE-798 Use of Hard-coded Credentials
       - SAP Security Patch Day July 2026
       - CVSS 9.1 (Critical) - unauthenticated, no privileges required
       - SAP Help Portal OAuth2 sample credentials (public documentation)
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="sap,commerce,initial_access,cve_2026_44761,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - SAP Commerce OAuth2 token endpoint base anchor
       Rule ID: 104175
       Matches any HTTP POST to the SAP Commerce authorization server
       OAuth2 token endpoint via Traefik JSON access logs.
       Level 5 - informational anchor used by frequency and chain rules.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104175" level="5">
    <decoded_as>json</decoded_as>
    <field name="RequestMethod">POST</field>
    <field name="RequestPath" type="pcre2">(?i)/authorizationserver/oauth/token</field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud: POST to OAuth2 token endpoint on $(RequestHost) from $(ClientHost) - CVE-2026-44761 exploitation anchor (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_token,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1078 / T1190  - Known sample client ID in OAuth2 request
       Rule ID: 104176
       Detects CVE-2026-44761 exploitation when the attacker passes
       a known hardcoded sample client_id (mobile_android,
       trusted_client, or client-side) as a URL query parameter
       in the POST to the OAuth2 token endpoint.
       Publicly documented sample credentials - no legitimate
       production use case for these client IDs.
       Level 14 - high confidence exploitation indicator.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104176" level="14">
    <decoded_as>json</decoded_as>
    <field name="RequestMethod">POST</field>
    <field name="RequestPath" type="pcre2">(?i)/authorizationserver/oauth/token.*client_id=(mobile_android|trusted_client|client-side)</field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud CVE-2026-44761: OAuth2 token request with known sample client ID on $(RequestHost) from $(ClientHost) - hardcoded credential abuse, investigate immediately (T1190, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_sample_client,cve_2026_44761,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - OAuth2 token endpoint successful response
       Rule ID: 104177
       Successful HTTP 200 response from the SAP Commerce OAuth2
       token endpoint indicates a token was issued. Any 200 response
       from this endpoint warrants investigation; combined with other
       indicators it signals active exploitation.
       Level 12 - investigate to determine if sample credentials used.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104177" level="12">
    <if_sid>104175</if_sid>
    <field name="DownstreamStatus" type="pcre2">^200$</field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud: OAuth2 token successfully issued from $(RequestHost) to $(ClientHost) - verify client credentials are not CVE-2026-44761 sample IDs (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_token_granted,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1078 / T1190  - Sample credential OAuth2 grant succeeded
       Rule ID: 104178
       OAuth2 token successfully issued (HTTP 200) when the request
       URL contains a known sample client ID. This is the highest-
       confidence CVE-2026-44761 exploitation indicator: the Commerce
       server issued a token to a publicly-known hardcoded credential.
       Level 15 - near-certain active exploitation, immediate response.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104178" level="15">
    <if_sid>104176</if_sid>
    <field name="DownstreamStatus" type="pcre2">^200$</field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud CVE-2026-44761 CONFIRMED: OAuth2 token granted to sample client ID on $(RequestHost) from $(ClientHost) - active hardcoded credential exploitation, immediate incident response required (T1190, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_sample_exploit_confirmed,cve_2026_44761,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - Burst of OAuth2 token requests (automated scanner)
       Rule ID: 104179
       Five or more POST requests to the SAP Commerce OAuth2 token
       endpoint from the same source IP within 60 seconds. This
       pattern indicates an automated exploit tool or credential
       scanner probing for CVE-2026-44761 sample credentials.
       Level 12 - automated CVE scanning activity.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104179" level="12" frequency="5" timeframe="60">
    <if_matched_sid>104175</if_matched_sid>
    <same_field>ClientHost</same_field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud: burst of 5+ OAuth2 token requests from $(ClientHost) in 60s - automated CVE-2026-44761 scanner or exploit tool probing sample credentials (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_burst,cve_2026_44761,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1530 / T1078  - SAP Commerce OCC API access
       Rule ID: 104180
       HTTP access to the SAP Commerce OCC (Omni Commerce Connect)
       REST API namespace (/occ/v2/). Post-exploitation, an attacker
       with a valid token from CVE-2026-44761 will call OCC endpoints
       to exfiltrate customer order data, product catalog, and pricing.
       Level 10 - potential post-exploitation data access; correlate
       with OAuth2 token endpoint activity.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104180" level="10">
    <decoded_as>json</decoded_as>
    <field name="RequestPath" type="pcre2">(?i)^/occ/v2/</field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud: OCC REST API access to $(RequestHost)$(RequestPath) from $(ClientHost) - correlate with CVE-2026-44761 OAuth2 token activity for post-exploitation data access (T1530, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1530</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_occ_api_access,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1530  - OCC API bulk enumeration from same source
       Rule ID: 104181
       Ten or more requests to the SAP Commerce OCC API namespace
       from the same source within 120 seconds. This pattern indicates
       automated data enumeration or exfiltration of customer orders,
       product catalog, or user accounts via a stolen OAuth2 token.
       Level 13 - bulk API data exfiltration pattern.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104181" level="13" frequency="10" timeframe="120">
    <if_matched_sid>104180</if_matched_sid>
    <same_field>ClientHost</same_field>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud OCC API bulk enumeration: 10+ requests to /occ/v2/ from $(ClientHost) in 120s - automated data exfiltration via stolen OAuth2 token, likely post-CVE-2026-44761 exploitation (T1530)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1530</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_occ_bulk_enum,cve_2026_44761,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190 / T1078  - Off-hours OAuth2 request to SAP Commerce
       Rule ID: 104182
       OAuth2 token request to the SAP Commerce authorization
       endpoint outside business hours. CVE-2026-44761 exploitation
       may occur after hours to avoid detection. Behavioral anomaly
       requiring analyst triage and correlation with other indicators.
       Level 9 - off-hours anomaly; investigate in context.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104182" level="9">
    <if_sid>104175</if_sid>
    <time>20:00 - 07:00</time>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud: OAuth2 token request outside business hours to $(RequestHost) from $(ClientHost) - off-hours anomaly; correlate with CVE-2026-44761 sample credential indicators (T1190, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_off_hours,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1078  - SAP Commerce application log: sample client OAuth2
       Rule ID: 104183
       Targets SAP Commerce hybris application logs (Java process log,
       Tomcat stdout, or hybris console log) forwarded to Wazuh.
       SAP Commerce logs OAuth2 token grants including the client_id.
       Matches log entries indicating a token was granted to one of
       the three publicly-known CVE-2026-44761 sample client IDs.
       Level 13 - application-layer confirmation of credential abuse.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104183" level="13">
    <program_name>^(hybris|tomcat|catalina|commerceserver|ycommerce)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(oauth.*token|token.*grant|access.?token.*(issu|grant|creat))[^\n]{0,200}(mobile_android|trusted_client|client-side)</regex>
    <description>SAP Commerce Cloud CVE-2026-44761: application log shows OAuth2 token granted to known sample client ID on $(hostname) - hardcoded credential abuse confirmed at application layer (T1078, T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1078</id>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>sap_oauth2_sample_client,cve_2026_44761,sap_app_log,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
